 ## Usage
 
+Run `tally <command>` (or `python -m tally <command>`) followed by any options.
+
 ```sh
-tally add 4.50 --category coffee
-tally list
-tally report
+tally add 4.50 coffee --note "morning flat white"
+tally list --limit 5
+tally report --month 2026-10
+tally export -o entries.csv
+```
+
+### Global options
+
+`tally --help` prints usage. `tally --version` prints the version.
+
+### `tally add` — record an expense (negative amount = refund)
+
+```
+usage: tally add [-h] [--note NOTE] [--date DATE] amount category
+```
+
+- `amount` — e.g. `4.50`, `"$4.50"`, `1,234.56` or `-12`
+- `category` — e.g. `coffee`, `groceries`, `rent`
+- `--note NOTE` — free-text note
+- `--date DATE` — `YYYY-MM-DD` (default: now)
+
+### `tally list` — show the most recent entries
+
+```
+usage: tally list [-h] [-n LIMIT]
 ```
 
+- `-n, --limit LIMIT` — how many entries (default: 10)
+
+### `tally report` — totals by category
+
+```
+usage: tally report [-h] [--month MONTH]
+```
+
+- `--month MONTH` — only this month, `YYYY-MM`
+
+### `tally export` — write all entries as CSV
+
+```
+usage: tally export [-h] [-o OUTPUT]
+```
+
+- `-o, --output OUTPUT` — file to write (default: stdout)
+
 Entries live in `~/.tallyho.json`. Set `TALLY_FILE` to use a different file.
 
